# HomeWeave Expo Cross-Platform Rules

Apply this rule when touching `apps/mobile/`, Expo configuration, platform adapters, notification or native build/release features.

- Use Expo-compatible package versions; prefer `npx expo install` for Expo/React Native dependencies and check compatibility against the project SDK.
- Keep platform-independent behavior in shared components/domain packages. Isolate required differences in `.web.tsx`, `.native.tsx`, `.ios.tsx`, `.android.tsx` or explicit platform adapters.
- Do not assume native APIs exist on Web. Check capability and provide a clear fallback.
- Never depend on the mobile app staying alive in the background for reliable household automation; those jobs belong on the backend.
- Implement loading, empty, error, offline, stale, unauthorized and partial-result UI states.
- Keep secrets out of client bundles. Use SecureStore for native-side sensitive tokens and secure server-managed sessions for Web.
- Test shared UI and domain behavior plus platform-specific paths. State clearly if simulator/device builds were not executed.
- Follow `docs/16_MOBILE_APP_ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/09_UI_UX_SPEC.md`.
